{"raw": {"https://wisconsin.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UW_Comprehensives/job/Menomonie-WI/Teaching-Assistant-Professor---Clinical-Mental-Health-Counseling-_JR10015085": {"title": "Teaching Assistant Professor \u2013 Clinical Mental Health Counseling", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-19\nFull time\n\nCurrent Employees: If you are currently employed at any of the Universities of Wisconsin, log in to Workday to apply through the internal application process. Position Title: Teaching Assistant Professor \u2013 Clinical Mental Health Counseling\u00a0 Job Category: Academic Staff Employment Type: Terminal (Fixed Term) Job Profile: Teaching Assistant Professor Job Duties: Teaching Assistant Professor \u2013 Clinical Mental Health Counseling\u00a0 \u00a0 The Department of Counseling, Rehabilitation, and Human Services is actively expanding their Clinical Mental Health Counseling (CMHC) program and seeking candidates for two Teaching Assistant Professor positions. \u00a0These grant-funded, full-time, 9-month academic year positions, with opportunity for summer work/teaching, may begin as soon as May 2027. \u00a0Faculty in these positions will initially give primary focus to curriculum development and CACREP accreditation alignment to assist in the development of an online part-time CMHC track. They will also teach within the current CMHC program. \u00a0Upon the successful launch of the part-time online program, the faculty responsibilities will transition to a four-four teaching load along with opportunities for service and scholarship responsibilities during the academic year with the opportunity for summer teaching for the remainder of the grant.\u00a0 \u00a0 These positions are reviewed annually with the intention to renew, contingent on grant funding, to September 2031. \u00a0At the culmination of grant funding, and depending on program success, the faculty may be eligible to apply for a tenure-track position, with potential for three years applied towards promotion and tenure, through the standard recruitment process. A successful candidate will be passionate about program and curriculum development, committed to promoting the development of an equitable and inclusive learning environment, and familiar with CACREP accreditation processes. The Department supports a variety of contemporary teaching modalities including in-person, blended, and distance learning environments. This position is supported by the Centers for Medicare & Medicaid Services (CMS) of the U.S. Department of Health and Human Services (HHS) through a subaward as part of a financial assistance award made to the State of Wisconsin Department of Health Services. The contents are those of the author(s) and do not necessarily represent the official views of, nor an endorsement, by CMS/HHS, or the U.S. Government. QUALIFICATIONS Minimum/Required \u00a0 MA/MS in Clinical Mental Health Counseling or related field Enrolled in a Doctorate Counseling Education & Supervision from a CACREP-accredited program (not applicable if Doctorate already obtained, see highly desired/preferred qualifications) Licensed or license-eligible as a licensed professional counselor in the state of Wisconsin Highly Desired/Preferred \u00a0 Doctorate in Counselor Education and Supervision from a CACREP-accredited program Two years\u2019 clinical experience post-graduation from MS/MA counseling program Evidence of successfully teaching in person and online Demonstrated ability to teach CMHC or closely related courses Familiarity with curriculum development Evidence of meaningful involvement in at least one CACREP accreditation/re-accreditation process Ability to collaborate and develop partnerships across campus and in the community RESPONSIBILITIES\u00a0 Assist with the development of the CMHC curriculum and program for online instruction Work closely with involved stakeholders to ensure the CMHC curriculum and program meet CACREP standards Engage in clinical practicum and internship site recruitment Teach in-person and/or online CMHC or related courses (e.g., Orientation to CMHC, Group Dynamics, Testing and Assessment, Diagnosis and Treatment, etc.) Provide in-person and remote clinical supervision Uphold an environment that supports a culture of respect, civility, and collegiality Actively participate in professional counseling organizations such as ACA, ACES, etc. Provide student academic advisement and conduct assessment of student learning. This includes contributing to academic program assessment, accreditation, and continuous improvement processes, in collaboration with faculty and staff. DEPARTMENT INFORMATION \u00a0 The Department of Counseling, Rehabilitation and Human Services is characterized by committed\u202f student-centered professionals who value teaching in a collaborative and participatory work environment.\u202fThe Department is committed to creating an inclusive campus community. Candidates who have experience working collaboratively with diverse individuals and/or groups and who can contribute to fostering an inclusive environment are encouraged to identify their experience in these areas. Graduates of the program are well-prepared to serve in a variety of diverse settings including public policy programs, mental health care agencies, schools and educational environments, non-profit organizations, Independent Living Centers, community-based agencies, hospital settings, and more. Program faculty also actively engage in collaborative scholarly work with campus, national, and international stakeholders. \u00a0 APPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS Complete applications received by end of day, Monday, November 23rd, 2026 are ensured full consideration. \u00a0Applications submitted after Monday, November 23rd, 2026 may be reviewed at the discretion of the search committee. To apply, click the APPLY button or go to: https://www.uwstout.edu/about-us/careers-jobs \u00a0 Due to system limitations, applicants may upload no more than five (5) attachments. Please combine documents where appropriate. Required application materials :\u00a0 Cover letter (* See below) Curriculum vitae or resume Teaching philosophy (single-spaced, maximum of two pages) Names and contact information for a minimum of three (3) professional references Unofficial copies of graduate transcripts\u00a0 * Please use your cover letter to speak to each of the Minimum/Required Qualifications for this position as listed above. For each required qualification, describe your relevant experience, using specific examples from your work history to illustrate how your experience satisfies the requirement. For questions regarding this position or recruitment, please contact: Search Chair: Andy Felton Phone: 715-232-2233 Email: feltonan@uwstout.edu If you need assistance with the online application process or if you submitted your application prior to uploading all of the required application materials, please contact: Search Coordinator: Alicia LaBonte Phone: 715-232-1282 Email: labontea@uwstout.edu Key Job Responsibilities: Contributes to the strategic development of curriculum and academic content through various mediums to ensure the integrity of the educational mission of the work unit Collaborates with department faculty and staff to develop teaching strategies relevant to the discipline Contributes to the development of teaching and learning scholarly work including publications and presentations Develops and designs curriculum and instructional material relevant to a course of instruction Facilitates classroom, online and/or laboratory instruction, including assessment of student performance Advises students on academic and career direction within a specific field of study May supervise student employees involved in development or delivery of instruction Guidelines to ensure consideration:\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Applicants must complete all required fields and attach all required application materials.\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Within your cover letter address each of the Minimum/Required Qualifications specified for this position. For each required qualification, describe your relevant experience, using specific examples from your work history to illustrate how your experience satisfies the requirement.\u00a0\u00a0 It is the policy of UW-Stout Polytechnic to provide reasonable accommodation to qualified applicants with disabilities. If you need assistance, or accommodation in applying because of a disability, please contact us using the information below. Employment opportunities will not be denied because of the need to make reasonable accommodation for a qualified individual's disability.\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 The Universities of Wisconsin provides an excellent benefits package including participation in the Wisconsin State retirement plan, demonstrating our commitment to the diverse needs of our employees.\u00a0 Employee Benefits:\u00a0 https://www.wisconsin.edu/ohrwd/benefits/ To calculate the estimated value of your total compensation, use the Health & Retirement Contributions Estimator | Employee Benefits (wisconsin.edu) Employment is contingent upon the final candidate\u2019s completing a criminal background check and being cleared to work by the Human Resources Office.\u00a0 Employment is also contingent upon the final candidate passing reference checks and an essential job function test, as applicable. The reference check process includes asking the final candidates\u2019 professional references questions regarding employee misconduct,\u00a0sexual violence,\u00a0and\u00a0sexual harassment. Reference checks must be conducted at a minimum with three professional references, at least one of which must be a prior supervisor. Final candidates with previous employment within the Universities of Wisconsin and State of WI agencies will be subject to additional reference checks.\u00a0 In response to a public records request, the Universities of Wisconsin will not reveal the identities of applicants who request confidentiality in their online application, except that the identity of the successful final candidate will be released. See Wis. Stat. sec. 19.36(7). UW-Stout Polytechnic is committed to providing safety and security of all members of our community in accordance with the Clery Act. For campus safety information and crime statistics visit: https://www.uwstout.edu/life-stout/police-and-parking/clery-information UW is an Equal Opportunity Employer Qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, pregnancy, disability, status as a protected veteran, or any other bases protected by applicable federal or State law and UW System policies. We are committed to building a workforce that represents a variety of backgrounds, perspectives, and skills, and encourage all qualified individuals to apply."}, "https://wisconsin.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UW_Comprehensives/job/Menomonie-WI/Assistant-Professor-of-Materials-Engineering_JR10014992": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Materials Engineering", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-15\nFull time\n\nCurrent Employees: If you are currently employed at any of the Universities of Wisconsin, log in to Workday to apply through the internal application process. Position Title: Assistant Professor of Materials Engineering Job Category: Faculty Employment Type: Regular Job Profile: Assistant Professor Job Duties: The Engineering and Technology Department invites applications for a position as a Materials Engineering Faculty member to prepare career-ready engineers and engineering technologists in alignment with UW-Stout\u2019s polytechnic tenets: applied learning and research, business and industry partnerships, and career focused education. We emphasize experiential learning by providing students with hands-on experiences in classroom, laboratory, and industrial settings. The Engineering and Technology Department at the University of Wisconsin-Stout Polytechnic offers six undergraduate programs, including Computer & Electrical Engineering, Manufacturing Engineering (B.S. and M.S.), Mechanical Engineering, Plastics Engineering, Engineering Technology, and Packaging. The successful candidate will be expected to teach in at least two of the areas listed in the Responsibilities section below. The anticipated start date is August 23, 2027. \u00a0 QUALIFICATIONS Minimum / Required Each of the following qualifications is required of all candidates: Ph.D. degree in Materials Engineering or related field by employment start date. Ability to teach in a combined lecture and lab environment. Fluency in oral and written English communication. Highly Desired/Preferred Preferred qualifications for this position are: 3 years combined industry, post-doctoral laboratory, teaching experience in materials engineering or related field. \u00a0 RESPONSIBILITIES Teach courses related to two or more of the following topics (depending on experience and qualifications): o\u00a0\u00a0 Materials Science and Engineering o\u00a0\u00a0 Metallurgy and Materials Processing o\u00a0\u00a0 Advanced and Emerging Engineering Materials o\u00a0\u00a0 Manufacturing and Materials Applications Establish and maintain laboratories and equipment. Develop and maintain contacts and liaison with industry and professional associations. Provide student academic advisement and conduct assessment of student learning. Contribute to academic program assessment and aid in maintaining program accreditation and continuous improvement in collaboration with faculty and staff. Develop curriculum. Actively engage in research. Participate in departmental and university service activities. \u00a0 \u00a0 DEPARTMENT INFORMATION The Engineering and Technology (E&T) Department is one of eight departments in the College of Science, Technology, Engineering, Mathematics, and Management (CSTEMM). The department has 30 full-time faculty and staff, four of whom are full-time technicians. The department provides courses for its well-established and accredited undergraduate programs in Computer & Electrical Engineering, Manufacturing Engineering (B.S. and M.S.), Mechanical Engineering, Plastics Engineering, Engineering Technology, and Packaging, plus other programs throughout the University. \u00a0 UW-Stout Polytechnic's Engineering and Technology Department values collaboration, innovation, and student success. Candidates with experience working collaboratively with a variety of individuals, groups, and community partners are encouraged to highlight those experiences in their application materials. \u00a0 APPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS Applications received by end of day, January 10, 2027 are ensured full consideration. \u00a0Applications submitted after January 10, 2027 may be reviewed at the discretion of the search committee. \u00a0 To apply, click on the APPLY button or go to: https://www.uwstout.edu/about-us/careers-jobs \u00a0 Due to system limitations, applicants may upload no more than five (5) attachments. Please combine documents where appropriate. \u00a0 Required application materials : Cover letter (* See below) Curriculum vitae or resume Teaching Philosophy (2 pages) Names and contact information for a minimum of three (3) professional references who can speak to your skills and abilities for the position \u00a0 * Please use your cover letter to speak to each of the Minimum/Required Qualifications for this position as listed above. For each required qualification, describe your relevant experience, using specific examples from your work history to illustrate how your experience satisfies the requirement. \u00a0 \u00a0 For questions regarding this position or recruitment, please contact: Search Chair: Alex Jordan Email: jordanal@uwstout.edu \u00a0 If you need assistance with the online application process or if you submitted your application prior to uploading all of the required application materials, please contact: Search Coordinator: Daisy Ramirez Email: ramirezda@uwstout.edu ADDITIONAL INFORMATION Key Job Responsibilities: Guidelines to ensure consideration:\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Applicants must complete all required fields and attach all required application materials.\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Within your cover letter address each of the Minimum/Required Qualifications specified for this position. For each required qualification, describe your relevant experience, using specific examples from your work history to illustrate how your experience satisfies the requirement.\u00a0\u00a0 It is the policy of UW-Stout Polytechnic to provide reasonable accommodation to qualified applicants with disabilities. If you need assistance, or accommodation in applying because of a disability, please contact us using the information below. Employment opportunities will not be denied because of the need to make reasonable accommodation for a qualified individual's disability.\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 The Universities of Wisconsin provides an excellent benefits package including participation in the Wisconsin State retirement plan, demonstrating our commitment to the diverse needs of our employees.\u00a0 Employee Benefits:\u00a0 https://www.wisconsin.edu/ohrwd/benefits/ To calculate the estimated value of your total compensation, use the Health & Retirement Contributions Estimator | Employee Benefits (wisconsin.edu) Employment is contingent upon the final candidate\u2019s completing a criminal background check and being cleared to work by the Human Resources Office.\u00a0 Employment is also contingent upon the final candidate passing reference checks and an essential job function test, as applicable. The reference check process includes asking the final candidates\u2019 professional references questions regarding employee misconduct,\u00a0sexual violence,\u00a0and\u00a0sexual harassment. Reference checks must be conducted at a minimum with three professional references, at least one of which must be a prior supervisor. Final candidates with previous employment within the Universities of Wisconsin and State of WI agencies will be subject to additional reference checks.\u00a0 In response to a public records request, the Universities of Wisconsin will not reveal the identities of applicants who request confidentiality in their online application, except that the identity of the successful final candidate will be released. See Wis. Stat. sec. 19.36(7). UW-Stout Polytechnic is committed to providing safety and security of all members of our community in accordance with the Clery Act. For campus safety information and crime statistics visit: https://www.uwstout.edu/life-stout/police-and-parking/clery-information UW is an Equal Opportunity Employer Qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, pregnancy, disability, status as a protected veteran, or any other bases protected by applicable federal or State law and UW System policies. We are committed to building a workforce that represents a variety of backgrounds, perspectives, and skills, and encourage all qualified individuals to apply."}, "https://wisconsin.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UW_Comprehensives/job/Menomonie-WI/Assistant-Professor-of-Mechanical-Engineering_JR10014993": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Mechanical Engineering", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-15\nFull time\n\nCurrent Employees: If you are currently employed at any of the Universities of Wisconsin, log in to Workday to apply through the internal application process. Position Title: Assistant Professor of Mechanical Engineering Job Category: Faculty Employment Type: Regular Job Profile: Assistant Professor Job Duties: Applications are invited for a tenure-track faculty position at the Assistant Professor rank in the Engineering & Technology Department at the University of Wisconsin-Stout Polytechnic. Our polytechnic tenets of applied learning, industry partnerships, and career-focused education emphasize hands-on student experiences in both classrooms and laboratories. The Engineering & Technology Department offers six undergraduate programs (B.S.): Computer and Electrical Engineering, Manufacturing Engineering, Mechanical Engineering, Plastics Engineering, Engineering Technology, and Packaging. All four engineering programs and the engineering technology program are ABET-accredited. The successful candidate will be expected to teach in at least two of the areas listed in the Responsibilities section below, primarily in the Mechanical Engineering program. The anticipated start date is August 23, 2027. \u00a0 QUALIFICATIONS Minimum / Required Each of the following qualifications is required of all candidates: Ph.D. degree in Mechanical Engineering or a related field by employment start date. At least 2 years of graduate-level research and/or industry experience in projects related to fluid mechanics and/or heat transfer Ability to teach in a combined lecture and lab environment. Fluency in oral and written English communication. Experience working in a collaborative environment \u00a0 Highly Desired/Preferred Preferred qualifications for this position are: 3 years of industry experience or undergraduate teaching experience or a combination of the two, in mechanical engineering or a related field Demonstrated commitment (workshops, courses, trainings, research projects, etc.) to advance innovative/evidence-based student learning \u00a0 RESPONSIBILITIES Teach courses related to two or more of the following topics (depending on experience and qualifications): o\u00a0\u00a0 Thermodynamics o\u00a0\u00a0 Heat transfer o\u00a0\u00a0 Fluid mechanics Establish and maintain laboratories and equipment. Develop and maintain contacts and liaison with industry and professional associations. Provide student academic advisement and conduct assessment of student learning. This includes contributing to academic program assessment, accreditation, and continuous improvement processes, in collaboration with faculty and staff. Develop curriculum. Actively engage in research. Participate in departmental and university service activities. \u00a0 DEPARTMENT INFORMATION The Engineering and Technology (E&T) Department is one of eight departments in the College of Science, Technology, Engineering, Mathematics, and Management (CSTEMM). The department has 30 full-time faculty and staff, four of whom are full-time technicians. The department provides courses for its well-established and accredited undergraduate programs in Computer & Electrical Engineering, Manufacturing Engineering (B.S. and M.S.), Mechanical Engineering, Plastics Engineering, Engineering Technology, and Packaging, plus other programs throughout the University. \u00a0 UW-Stout Polytechnic's Engineering and Technology Department values collaboration, innovation, and student success. Candidates with experience working collaboratively with a variety of individuals, groups, and community partners are encouraged to highlight those experiences in their application materials. \u00a0 APPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS \u00a0 Applications received by end of day, Monday, January 11th, 2027, will be given full consideration. \u00a0Applications submitted after January 11th, 2027, may be reviewed at the search committee's discretion. \u00a0 To apply, click on the APPLY button or go to: https://www.uwstout.edu/about-us/careers-jobs \u00a0 Due to system limitations, applicants may upload no more than five (5) attachments. Please combine documents where appropriate. \u00a0 Required application materials : Cover letter (maximum 2 pages, *see below) Curriculum vitae or resume Teaching Philosophy (maximum 2 pages) Names and contact information for a minimum of three (3) professional references who can speak to your skills and abilities for the position \u00a0 * Please use your cover letter to speak to each of the Minimum/Required as well as Highly Desired/Preferred Qualifications for this position as listed above. For each required qualification, describe your relevant experience, using specific examples from your work/academic history to illustrate how your experience satisfies the requirement. \u00a0 Official transcripts will be required at time of hire. \u00a0 For questions regarding this position or recruitment, please contact: Search Chair: Abhimanyu Ghosh Email: ghosha@uwstout.edu \u00a0 If you need assistance with the online application process or if you submitted your application prior to uploading all the required application materials, please contact: Search Coordinator: Lara Lange Email: langela@uwstout.edu \u00a0 ADDITIONAL INFORMATION \u00a0 Competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience. Key Job Responsibilities: Guidelines to ensure consideration:\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Applicants must complete all required fields and attach all required application materials.\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Within your cover letter address each of the Minimum/Required Qualifications specified for this position. For each required qualification, describe your relevant experience, using specific examples from your work history to illustrate how your experience satisfies the requirement.\u00a0\u00a0 It is the policy of UW-Stout Polytechnic to provide reasonable accommodation to qualified applicants with disabilities. If you need assistance, or accommodation in applying because of a disability, please contact us using the information below. Employment opportunities will not be denied because of the need to make reasonable accommodation for a qualified individual's disability.\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 The Universities of Wisconsin provides an excellent benefits package including participation in the Wisconsin State retirement plan, demonstrating our commitment to the diverse needs of our employees.\u00a0 Employee Benefits:\u00a0 https://www.wisconsin.edu/ohrwd/benefits/ To calculate the estimated value of your total compensation, use the Health & Retirement Contributions Estimator | Employee Benefits (wisconsin.edu) Employment is contingent upon the final candidate\u2019s completing a criminal background check and being cleared to work by the Human Resources Office.\u00a0 Employment is also contingent upon the final candidate passing reference checks and an essential job function test, as applicable. The reference check process includes asking the final candidates\u2019 professional references questions regarding employee misconduct,\u00a0sexual violence,\u00a0and\u00a0sexual harassment. Reference checks must be conducted at a minimum with three professional references, at least one of which must be a prior supervisor. Final candidates with previous employment within the Universities of Wisconsin and State of WI agencies will be subject to additional reference checks.\u00a0 In response to a public records request, the Universities of Wisconsin will not reveal the identities of applicants who request confidentiality in their online application, except that the identity of the successful final candidate will be released. See Wis. Stat. sec. 19.36(7). UW-Stout Polytechnic is committed to providing safety and security of all members of our community in accordance with the Clery Act. For campus safety information and crime statistics visit: https://www.uwstout.edu/life-stout/police-and-parking/clery-information UW is an Equal Opportunity Employer Qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, pregnancy, disability, status as a protected veteran, or any other bases protected by applicable federal or State law and UW System policies. We are committed to building a workforce that represents a variety of backgrounds, perspectives, and skills, and encourage all qualified individuals to apply."}, "https://wisconsin.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UW_Comprehensives/job/Menomonie-WI/Assistant-Professor-of-Industrial-Organizational-Psychology_JR10015652": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Industrial/Organizational Psychology", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-07\nFull time\n\nCurrent Employees: If you are currently employed at any of the Universities of Wisconsin, log in to Workday to apply through the internal application process. Position Title: Assistant Professor of Industrial/Organizational Psychology Job Category: Faculty Employment Type: Regular Job Profile: Assistant Professor Job Duties: The University of Wisconsin-Stout Polytechnic Psychology Department is seeking applicants with an industrial/organizational psychology background for a tenure-track assistant professor position, starting August 23, 2027. \u00a0 As a teaching- and application-focused campus, we are seeking someone who is excited to engage in active learning experiences with our undergraduate and graduate students. The qualified candidate will teach courses such as Personnel Psychology, Organizational Psychology, Occupational Health Psychology, Industrial/Organizational Psychology Consulting, Human Resource Management, and courses related to the qualified candidate\u2019s expertise areas, as needed. The qualified candidate will also be expected to engage in research, mentor and advise undergraduate students, and engage in service to the profession, department, and/or university. UW-Stout provides numerous opportunities for faculty to continually develop and improve on the quality of their teaching skills by offering on- and off-campus professional development experiences each year. \u00a0 QUALIFICATIONS Minimum / Required A doctorate in Industrial/Organizational Psychology or a closely related field by employment start date (August 23, 2027). Commitment to teaching undergraduate- and graduate-level courses in psychology, especially in I/O psychology and human resources. \u00a0 Highly Desired/Preferred Applicants should ideally be able to demonstrate evidence of experience or interest in: developing an active psychology research program involving undergraduate and graduate students. academic advisement. a commitment to service at the department and university level. \u00a0 RESPONSIBILITIES UW-Stout is a primarily teaching institution with faculty teaching typically 24 credits per academic year. Psychology department faculty are expected to teach a variety of courses in both in-person and online formats in their discipline within the psychology department and to provide student academic advisement. Faculty are expected to conduct assessment of student learning, which includes contributing to academic program assessment, accreditation, and continuous improvement processes, in collaboration with faculty and staff. Faculty members are also expected to engage in scholarship and participate in departmental, university, and professional service to support continuous improvement and a culture of collegiality and civility. \u00a0 DEPARTMENT INFORMATION The\u00a0 Psychology Department 's purpose is to engage its faculty and students in discovery, critical thinking, and self-development in order to foster growth as enlightened citizens, able to enrich lives in local and global communities. The department offers a bachelor\u2019s degree in psychology , which as of Spring 2026 was the most popular major in the College of Arts and Human Sciences, and a growing online master's degree in Applied Industrial/Organizational Psychology . It also has a dedicated experimental laboratory space. Candidates who have experience and an interest in fostering an inclusive environment are strongly encouraged to apply. Collaborative relationships and inclusion are valued in this department. \u00a0 APPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS \u00a0 Complete applications received by end of day, Sunday, November 8, 2026 are ensured full consideration. \u00a0Applications submitted after November 8, 2026 may be reviewed at the discretion of the search committee or until position is filled. \u00a0 To apply, click on the APPLY button or go to: https://www.uwstout.edu/about-us/careers-jobs \u00a0 Due to system limitations, applicants may upload no more than five (5) attachments. Please combine documents where appropriate. \u00a0 Required application materials : Cover letter (* See below) Curriculum vitae or resume Statement of teaching philosophy and (if applicable) evidence of teaching effectiveness (e.g., course evaluations, peer evaluations, etc.) Unofficial copies of graduate transcripts (official transcripts required at time of hire) Names and contact information for a minimum of three (3) professional references who can speak to your skills and abilities for the position \u00a0 * Please use your cover letter to speak to each of the Minimum/Required and Highly Desired/Preferred Qualifications for this position as listed above. For each qualification, describe your relevant experience, using specific examples from your work history to illustrate how your experience satisfies the requirement. \u00a0 For questions regarding this position or recruitment, please contact: Search Chair: Dana Linnell, PhD Phone: 715-232-5293 Email: linnellda@uwstout.edu \u00a0 If you need assistance with the online application process or if you submitted your application prior to uploading all the required application materials, please contact: Search Coordinator: AJ Ja Doul Phone: 715-232-1681 Email: jadoula@uwstout.edu \u00a0 ADDITIONAL INFORMATION \u00a0 Competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience. Key Job Responsibilities: Guidelines to ensure consideration:\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Applicants must complete all required fields and attach all required application materials.\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Within your cover letter address each of the Minimum/Required Qualifications specified for this position. For each required qualification, describe your relevant experience, using specific examples from your work history to illustrate how your experience satisfies the requirement.\u00a0\u00a0 It is the policy of UW-Stout Polytechnic to provide reasonable accommodation to qualified applicants with disabilities. If you need assistance, or accommodation in applying because of a disability, please contact us using the information below. Employment opportunities will not be denied because of the need to make reasonable accommodation for a qualified individual's disability.\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 The Universities of Wisconsin provides an excellent benefits package including participation in the Wisconsin State retirement plan, demonstrating our commitment to the diverse needs of our employees.\u00a0 Employee Benefits:\u00a0 https://www.wisconsin.edu/ohrwd/benefits/ To calculate the estimated value of your total compensation, use the Health & Retirement Contributions Estimator | Employee Benefits (wisconsin.edu) Employment is contingent upon the final candidate\u2019s completing a criminal background check and being cleared to work by the Human Resources Office.\u00a0 Employment is also contingent upon the final candidate passing reference checks and an essential job function test, as applicable. The reference check process includes asking the final candidates\u2019 professional references questions regarding employee misconduct,\u00a0sexual violence,\u00a0and\u00a0sexual harassment. Reference checks must be conducted at a minimum with three professional references, at least one of which must be a prior supervisor. Final candidates with previous employment within the Universities of Wisconsin and State of WI agencies will be subject to additional reference checks.\u00a0 In response to a public records request, the Universities of Wisconsin will not reveal the identities of applicants who request confidentiality in their online application, except that the identity of the successful final candidate will be released. See Wis. Stat. sec. 19.36(7). UW-Stout Polytechnic is committed to providing safety and security of all members of our community in accordance with the Clery Act. For campus safety information and crime statistics visit: https://www.uwstout.edu/life-stout/police-and-parking/clery-information UW is an Equal Opportunity Employer Qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, pregnancy, disability, status as a protected veteran, or any other bases protected by applicable federal or State law and UW System policies. We are committed to building a workforce that represents a variety of backgrounds, perspectives, and skills, and encourage all qualified individuals to apply."}, "https://wisconsin.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UW_Comprehensives/job/Menomonie-WI/Teaching-Assistant-Associate-Professor---Master-s-in-Social-Work_JR10015087": {"title": "Teaching Assistant/Associate Professor \u2013 Master's in Social Work", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-06\nFull time\n\nCurrent Employees: If you are currently employed at any of the Universities of Wisconsin, log in to Workday to apply through the internal application process. Position Title: Teaching Assistant/Associate Professor \u2013 Master's in Social Work Job Category: Academic Staff Employment Type: Terminal (Fixed Term) Job Profile: Teaching Assistant Professor Job Duties: The Department of Counseling, Rehabilitation, and Human Services is actively expanding their department and developing a master\u2019s in Social Work degree and seeking candidates for four Teaching Assistant/Associate Professor positions. \u00a0These grant-funded, full-time, 9-month academic year positions, with opportunity for summer work/teaching may begin as soon as January 2027.\u00a0 Faculty in these positions will initially give primary focus on curriculum development, CSWE accreditation alignment.\u00a0 We are seeking candidates for leadership roles within the program to assist in the development of a part-time hybrid MSW program along with teaching within similar disciplines. Upon successful program launching, the faculty responsibilities will transition to a four-four teaching load during the academic year with opportunities for scholarship and service responsibilities, and opportunities for summer teaching for the remainder of the grant. \u00a0 These positions are non-tenure track, reviewed annually with the intention to renew, contingent on grant funding, through September 2031.\u00a0 At culmination of grant funding and depending on program success, the faculty may be eligible to apply for a tenure track position, with potential for three years applied towards promotion and tenure, through the standard recruitment process. \u00a0 A successful candidate will be passionate about program and curriculum development, committed to promoting the development of an equitable and inclusive learning environment, and familiar with CSWE accreditation processes. The Department supports a variety of contemporary teaching modalities including in-person, blended, and distance learning environments. \u00a0 This position is supported by the Centers for Medicare & Medicaid Services (CMS) of the U.S. Department of Health and Human Services (HHS) through a subaward as part of a financial assistance award made to the State of Wisconsin Department of Health Services. The contents are those of the author(s) and do not necessarily represent the official views of, nor an endorsement, by CMS/HHS, or the U.S. Government. \u00a0 QUALIFICATIONS Minimum/Required Master\u2019s in Social Work from a CSWE-accredited program Licensed or license eligible as a social worker in the state of Wisconsin Highly Desired/Preferred Enrolled in or completed PhD in Social Work or closely related professional degree Two years' experience working in the social work profession with emphasis on macro-scale interventions Ability to successfully teach in-person and online Demonstrate ability to teach Social Work or closely related courses Articulated interest in leadership roles and skills for successful leadership within the program (i.e. Program Director, Field Director) Familiarity with curriculum development Demonstrated knowledge of or experience with of the CSWE accreditation requirements and process Demonstrated collaboration and partnership development across campus and in the community \u00a0 RESPONSIBILITIES Assist with the development of CSWE aligned curriculum and program for hybrid instruction. Work closely with involved stakeholders to ensure Social Work curriculum and program meet CSWE standards. Engage in clinical practicum and internship site recruitment Engage in student recruitment Possible leadership responsibilities within the program (i.e. Program Director or Field Director) Teach on campus and online Social Work or closely related courses Provide on-campus and remote clinical supervision. Uphold an environment that supports a culture of respect, civility, and collegiality. Actively participate in professional social work organizations such as NASW, APHA, etc. Provide student academic advisement and conduct assessment of student learning. This includes contributing to academic program assessment, accreditation, and continuous improvement processes, in collaboration with faculty and staff. \u00a0 DEPARTMENT INFORMATION The Department of Counseling, Rehabilitation and Human Services is characterized by committed\u00a0student-centered professionals who value teaching in a collaborative and participatory work environment.\u00a0The Department is committed to creating an inclusive campus community. Candidates who have experience working collaboratively with diverse individuals and/or groups and who can contribute to fostering an inclusive environment are encouraged to identify their experience in these areas. Graduates of the program are well-prepared to serve in a variety of diverse settings including public policy programs, mental health care agencies, schools and educational environments, non-profit organizations, Independent Living Centers, community-based agencies, hospital settings, and more. Program faculty also actively engage in collaborative scholarly work with campus, national, and international stakeholders. \u00a0 APPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS \u00a0 Complete applications received by end of day, Sunday, November 8, 2026 are ensured full consideration. \u00a0Applications submitted after November 8, 2026 may be reviewed at the discretion of the search committee. \u00a0 To apply, click on the APPLY button or go to: https://www.uwstout.edu/about-us/careers-jobs \u00a0 Due to system limitations, applicants may upload no more than five (5) attachments. Please combine documents where appropriate. \u00a0 Required application materials : Cover letter (* See below) Curriculum vitae or resume Teaching Philosophy (single spaced, two pages max) Names and contact information for a minimum of three (3) professional references Unofficial copies of graduate transcripts \u00a0 * Please use your cover letter to speak to each of the Minimum/Required Qualifications for this position as listed above. For each required qualification, describe your relevant experience, using specific examples from your work history to illustrate how your experience satisfies the requirement. \u00a0 For questions regarding this position or recruitment, please contact: Search Chair: Andy Felton Email: feltonan@uwstout.edu \u00a0 If you need assistance with the online application process or if you submitted your application prior to uploading all of the required application materials, please contact: Search Coordinator: Alicia LaBonte Email: labontea@uwstout.edu INSTITUTIONAL OVERVIEW\u00a0 Key Job Responsibilities: Advises students on academic and career direction within a specific field of study Develops and designs curriculum and instructional material relevant to a course of instruction Facilitates classroom, online and/or laboratory instruction, including assessment of student performance Collaborates with department faculty and staff to develop teaching strategies relevant to the discipline May supervise student employees involved in development or delivery of instruction Contributes to the development of teaching and learning scholarly work including publications and presentations Contributes to the strategic development of curriculum and academic content through various mediums to ensure the integrity of the educational mission of the work unit Guidelines to ensure consideration:\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Applicants must complete all required fields and attach all required application materials.\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Within your cover letter address each of the Minimum/Required Qualifications specified for this position. For each required qualification, describe your relevant experience, using specific examples from your work history to illustrate how your experience satisfies the requirement.\u00a0\u00a0 It is the policy of UW-Stout Polytechnic to provide reasonable accommodation to qualified applicants with disabilities. If you need assistance, or accommodation in applying because of a disability, please contact us using the information below. Employment opportunities will not be denied because of the need to make reasonable accommodation for a qualified individual's disability.\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 The Universities of Wisconsin provides an excellent benefits package including participation in the Wisconsin State retirement plan, demonstrating our commitment to the diverse needs of our employees.\u00a0 Employee Benefits:\u00a0 https://www.wisconsin.edu/ohrwd/benefits/ To calculate the estimated value of your total compensation, use the Health & Retirement Contributions Estimator | Employee Benefits (wisconsin.edu) Employment is contingent upon the final candidate\u2019s completing a criminal background check and being cleared to work by the Human Resources Office.\u00a0 Employment is also contingent upon the final candidate passing reference checks and an essential job function test, as applicable. The reference check process includes asking the final candidates\u2019 professional references questions regarding employee misconduct,\u00a0sexual violence,\u00a0and\u00a0sexual harassment. Reference checks must be conducted at a minimum with three professional references, at least one of which must be a prior supervisor. Final candidates with previous employment within the Universities of Wisconsin and State of WI agencies will be subject to additional reference checks.\u00a0 In response to a public records request, the Universities of Wisconsin will not reveal the identities of applicants who request confidentiality in their online application, except that the identity of the successful final candidate will be released. See Wis. Stat. sec. 19.36(7). UW-Stout Polytechnic is committed to providing safety and security of all members of our community in accordance with the Clery Act. For campus safety information and crime statistics visit: https://www.uwstout.edu/life-stout/police-and-parking/clery-information UW is an Equal Opportunity Employer Qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, pregnancy, disability, status as a protected veteran, or any other bases protected by applicable federal or State law and UW System policies. We are committed to building a workforce that represents a variety of backgrounds, perspectives, and skills, and encourage all qualified individuals to apply."}, "https://wisconsin.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UW_Comprehensives/job/Menomonie-WI/Lecturer-of-Early-Childhood-Education_JR10009647": {"title": "Lecturer of Early Childhood Education", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-27\nFull time\n\nCurrent Employees: If you are currently employed at any of the Universities of Wisconsin, log in to Workday to apply through the internal application process. Position Title: Lecturer of Early Childhood Education Job Category: Academic Staff Employment Type: Terminal (Fixed Term) Job Profile: Lecturer Job Duties: The University of Wisconsin-Stout, Wisconsin\u2019s Polytechnic University, is seeking an emerging or established scholar that is passionate and committed to promoting the development of equitable, inclusive, and quality teaching and learning in early childhood education. The B.S. in Early Childhood Education program at UW-Stout is renowned for its commitment to research-based, developmentally appropriate and applied learning practices. Early Childhood Education at UW-Stout is in the Department of Teaching, Learning, and Leadership and one of the signature educator preparation programs at the university that leads to licensure in Early Childhood Education (birth to grade 3) and Early Childhood Special Education (birth to grade 3). The successful candidate will teach undergraduate courses (face-to-face and online), including teacher preparation, supervision of student teachers, and program assessment of student learning with teaching opportunities during the summer. The anticipated start date is the Spring 2027 semester: Thursday, December 31, 2026. QUALIFICATIONS Minimum / Required An earned Master\u2019s degree in Early Childhood Education or related field by employment start date. At least three (3) years of full-time teaching experience as the lead teacher in Birth-Age 8 range. Licensable in Early Childhood Education and/or Early Childhood Special Education in Birth-Age 8 range. Highly Desired/Preferred At least one degree earned in Early Childhood Education and/or Early Childhood Special Education A record of strong teaching of teacher education courses. A record of supervision of Early Childhood Education teacher candidates. Demonstrated commitment to student success. RESPONSIBILITIES Teach Early Childhood Education and/or Early Childhood Special Education courses; supervise teacher candidates in field experiences; provide student academic advisement and conduct assessment of student learning; develop and maintain positive relations with outside agencies; demonstrate ability to work collaboratively with faculty and staff as well as independently contributing to academic program assessment and continuous improvement processes; interest in advancing student learning in the area of early childhood education and in alignment with UW-Stout\u2019s polytechnic tenets of applied learning and research, business and industry partnerships, career focused education. DEPARTMENT INFORMATION The mission of the Teaching, Learning, and Leadership (TLL) Department is to provide exemplary teaching, research, and service to ensure graduates become successful and effective leaders in their chosen professional discipline. To meet this mission, faculty and staff are expected to: Foster the development of educational professionals engaged in reflective practice. Provide program curricula reflecting diversity, research, theory, and best practice. Align program outcomes with federal, state, and national education standards. Recruit, support, and retain diverse faculty and staff who model best practices in professional education. Advance educational scholarship and research at the university, local, state, national, and international levels. Collaborate with the Child and Family Study Center (CFSC) and pK-12 schools, universities, technical colleges, educational agencies, professional associations, and communities to improve teaching and learning. Engage in leadership and service to the university, local, state, national, and international professional organizations. Provide student academic advisement and conduct assessment of student learning. This includes contributing to academic program assessment, accreditation, and continuous improvement processes, in collaboration with faculty and staff. APPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS Complete applications received by end of day, September 28, 2026 are ensured full consideration. \u00a0Applications submitted after September 28, 2026 may be reviewed at the discretion of the search committee or until position is filled. To apply, click on the APPLY button or go to: https://www.uwstout.edu/about-us/careers-jobs Due to system limitations, applicants may upload no more than five (5) attachments. Please combine documents where appropriate. Required application materials : Cover letter (* See below) Curriculum vitae or resume Statement of Teaching Philosophy (1-2 pages) Names and contact information for a minimum of three (3) professional references who can speak to your skills and abilities for the position * Please use your cover letter to speak to each of the Minimum/Required Qualifications for this position as listed above. For each required qualification, describe your relevant experience, using specific examples from your work history to illustrate how your experience satisfies the requirement. Applicants must complete all required fields and attach all required documents prior to submitting the online application. Note: Once you have attached your materials and submitted your application you will not be able to go into the system and change them. Before starting the online application process, we recommend you preview the frequently asked questions (FAQs) available at: https://kb.uwss.wisconsin.edu/21900 For questions regarding this position or recruitment, please contact: Search Chair: Lindsay Barnhart Phone: 715-232-5511 Email: barnhartl@uwstout.edu If you need assistance with the online application process or if you submitted your application prior to uploading all the required application materials, please contact: Search Coordinator: Ann Cummings Phone: 715-232-5632 Email: larsenan@uwstout.edu ADDITIONAL INFORMATION Competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience. Official transcripts required at time of hire. Key Job Responsibilities: Develops instructional design and curriculum relevant to a course of instruction Serves as an initial point of contact for students as it relates to specific course or series content and expectations Facilitates classroom, online and/or laboratory instruction for one or more courses, including assessment of student performance Guidelines to ensure consideration:\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Applicants must complete all required fields and attach all required application materials.\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Within your cover letter address each of the Minimum/Required Qualifications specified for this position. For each required qualification, describe your relevant experience, using specific examples from your work history to illustrate how your experience satisfies the requirement.\u00a0\u00a0 It is the policy of UW-Stout Polytechnic to provide reasonable accommodation to qualified applicants with disabilities. If you need assistance, or accommodation in applying because of a disability, please contact us using the information below. Employment opportunities will not be denied because of the need to make reasonable accommodation for a qualified individual's disability.\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 The Universities of Wisconsin provides an excellent benefits package including participation in the Wisconsin State retirement plan, demonstrating our commitment to the diverse needs of our employees.\u00a0 Employee Benefits:\u00a0 https://www.wisconsin.edu/ohrwd/benefits/ To calculate the estimated value of your total compensation, use the Health & Retirement Contributions Estimator | Employee Benefits (wisconsin.edu) Employment is contingent upon the final candidate\u2019s completing a criminal background check and being cleared to work by the Human Resources Office.\u00a0 Employment is also contingent upon the final candidate passing reference checks and an essential job function test, as applicable. The reference check process includes asking the final candidates\u2019 professional references questions regarding employee misconduct,\u00a0sexual violence,\u00a0and\u00a0sexual harassment. Reference checks must be conducted at a minimum with three professional references, at least one of which must be a prior supervisor. Final candidates with previous employment within the Universities of Wisconsin and State of WI agencies will be subject to additional reference checks.\u00a0 In response to a public records request, the Universities of Wisconsin will not reveal the identities of applicants who request confidentiality in their online application, except that the identity of the successful final candidate will be released. See Wis. Stat. sec. 19.36(7). UW-Stout Polytechnic is committed to providing safety and security of all members of our community in accordance with the Clery Act. For campus safety information and crime statistics visit: https://www.uwstout.edu/life-stout/police-and-parking/clery-information UW is an Equal Opportunity Employer Qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, pregnancy, disability, status as a protected veteran, or any other bases protected by applicable federal or State law and UW System policies. We are committed to building a workforce that represents a variety of backgrounds, perspectives, and skills, and encourage all qualified individuals to apply."}}, "rows": {"https://wisconsin.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UW_Comprehensives/job/Menomonie-WI/Teaching-Assistant-Professor---Clinical-Mental-Health-Counseling-_JR10015085": {"school_id": 1545, "posting_url": "https://wisconsin.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UW_Comprehensives/job/Menomonie-WI/Teaching-Assistant-Professor---Clinical-Mental-Health-Counseling-_JR10015085", "job_title_in_post": "Teaching Assistant Professor \u2013 Clinical Mental Health Counseling", "position_type": "Assistant_Professor", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "Department of Health Services", "area_key_words": "Clinical Menta